# Whole-words prose (always on)

Before sending a user-facing reply or editing `ports/verified-architecture/**/*.md`:

1. Expand acronyms to full phrases (`Model Context Protocol`, not bare `MCP`).
2. Follow Skill `whole-words-prose` and `ports/verified-architecture/GLOSSARY.md`.
3. Human decision questions must name concrete day-90 outcomes, not tautological
   slogan pairs (“verify spine vs brownfield MCP”).
4. Prefer Skill `predicate-prose` tests so bullets change allowed next actions.

Exceptions: paths, fenced code, one short form after a full phrase, or typed
choice tokens that are expanded in the same bullet.
